    "id": "hunt-lifting-cycle-settles-as-one-signature",
    "category": "name-resolution",
    "source": "C = B + z\nA = {\n  H = B + 0\n  x + 1\n}\nB = y + A\nC(1, 2, 3)",
    "outcome": "Evaluates",
    "displayChecks": [
      {
        "text": "7"
      }
    ],
    "expectedRaw": "7",
    "expectedEmittedCount": 1,
    "explanation": "The nested helper `H` lifts `B` and captures `A`'s `x`. The output of `A(x)` is `x + 1`, so `B(y, x)` computes `y + (x + 1)` and `C(z, y, x)` adds `z`. The call gives `2 + (3 + 1) + 1`."
